dialect protocol
protocol stdio.semio.model.snapshot
version 1
schema stdio.semio.model
start body
framing record

# P2 pilot (model): REAL binary pack frame, replacing the old `serde_json::to_vec`-in-envelope
# shortcut (`📸️snapshot/🦀️.rs`'s old `ArtifactPack::encode_pack_with`). `format u8` (real,
# fixed) then `schema_len`/`schema_bytes` (real, varint-length-prefixed UTF-8 — matches
# `write_str_lp`'s own wire exactly) are genuinely, fully described. Past that, `spatial`/
# `elements`/`relations` are HOMOGENEOUS but variable-length repeated records (`SpatialNode`/
# `SemioModelElement`/`ModelRelation`, each itself holding further nested variable-length fields —
# `psets`, `properties`, tagged enum payloads) — the `protocol-array-of-records` gap (`repeat`'s own
# arms are tag-dispatched, not "repeat N times, N from a count field", for an untagged homogeneous
# record): modeled as one opaque trailing `payload` chain, the same honest boundary every P1-P3
# pilot's own nested/recursive payload uses. The real Rust `encode_model_snapshot_binary`/
# `decode_model_snapshot_binary` stays genuinely, fully structured (varint counts, per-field
# length-prefixes, real `f64` LE coordinates, u8 enum tags) — round-trip tested independently by
# this facet's own tests, only the protocol DESCRIPTION stops at this boundary.
header fixed 1
field format u8

segment schema_len varint
segment schema_bytes Array(u8, Field(schema_len))

chain payload bytes
